  "hypothesis": {
    "text": "it was impressive to have no speed and high regeneration; melee damage first half, attack speed second half; a bit of armor/dodge",
    "recorded_at": "2026-09-02T16:39:58.135Z"
  },
  "diagnosis": {
    "text": "Bait carried the run, not the stat shaping: 49 free Baits are 392 of the 408 percent damage and 98 of the 132 harvesting, so the melee-then-attack-speed layering was multiplying a base the character had already been handed. The melee/attack-speed split is real (melee 2->45 by wave 12 with attack speed still 0; attack speed 4->99 from wave 10 on), but regeneration was 0 until wave 15 and only reached 11 at wave 20, so it explains nothing about the run's shape. The mid-game health dips - 11 hp entering wave 10, 17 entering wave 13 - are the extra-enemy cost of the Bait stack outrunning the attack speed available to clear it; only from wave 14, at 49 attack speed, did damage per wave go vertical (30k -> 46k -> 57k -> 84k -> 93k -> 172k).",
    "recorded_at": "2026-09-02T16:41:29.037Z"
  },
  "change": {
    "text": "Next Fisherman run, reach 50 attack speed by wave 10: in the wave 8-10 shops buy attack speed ahead of any percent damage, since Bait supplies the percent damage for free.",
    "recorded_at": "2026-09-02T16:41:29.038Z"
  },
